imālaya) demanded that the sun should revolve round himself as about Meru, which the sun declined to do; whereupon the Vindhya began to rise higher and higher so as to obstruct the path of the sun and moon. The gods being alarmed sought the aid of the sage Agastya, who approached the mountain and requested that by bending down he would give him an easy passage to the south, and that he would retain the same position till his return. This Vindhya consented to do (because according to one account, he regarded Agastya as his teacher); but Agastya never returned from the south, and Vindhya never attained the height of Meru.]"}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A hunter."}]},{"n":4,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"न्ध्या N. of a plant (लवली)."}]},{"n":5,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Small cardamoms."}]},{"n":6,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A measure of time (त्रुटि); L. D. B. -Comp. -अटवी the great Vindhya forest. -कूटः, -कूटनम् epithets of the sage Agastya.-गिरिः the Vindhya range of hills; also विन्ध्याचल, विन्ध्याद्रि. -वासिन् m. an epithet of the grammarian व्याडि. (-नी) an epithet of Durgā."}]}]}],"vinakaH":[{"id":"vinnakaH","headword":"विन्नकः","headword_slp1":"vinnakaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"विन्नकः [vinnakḥ], N. of Agastya."}]}]}],"vinyasanam":[{"id":"vinyasanam","headword":"विन्यसनम्","headword_slp1":"vinyasanam","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"विन्यसनम् [vinyasanam], Putting down; पदविन्यसनम्. See न्यास."}]}]}],"vinyas":[{"id":"vinyas","headword":"विन्यस्","headword_slp1":"vinyas","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"विन्यस् [vinyas], 4 P."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To put down, deposit, place; विन्यस्यन्ती भुवि गणनया देहलीदत्तपुष्पैः "},{"t":"cite","s":"Me.89","q":"Me"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"Bk.3.3","q":"Bk"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To fix in or on, direct towards; रामे विन्यस्तमानसाः Rām."}]},{"n":4,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"To deliver or make over, commit to the care of, entrust; सु